Given the complex number $z=a^2-7a+6+(a^2-5a-6)i$ ($a\in\mathbb{R}$), find the values of the real number $a$ for which $z$ is:  
(1) a real number;  
(2) an imaginary number;  
(3) a pure imaginary number.

Given the expression $(x^2+ \frac {2}{x})^n$, where $n\in\mathbb{N}^*$.  
(Ⅰ) When $n=6$, find the constant term in the binomial expansion;  
(Ⅱ) If the binomial coefficient of the third term is equal to the binomial coefficient of the seventh term in the expansion of $(x^2+ \frac {2}{x})^n$, find the coefficient of the middle term in the expansion.

Define a new operation, observe the following expressions:  
$1\odot 3=1\times 2+3=5$, $4\odot \left(-1\right)=4\times 2-1=7$;  
$(-2)\odot 3=\left(-2\right)\times 2+3=-1$; $6\odot 5=6\times 2+5=17$; $\ldots$  
$(1)$ Please think about: Express $x\odot y$ with an algebraic expression as ______;  
$(2)$ If $a\odot \left(-6b\right)=4$, calculate the value of $\left(a-5b\right)\odot \left(a+b\right)$.

Given the function $f(x)=A\sin ^{2}(ωx+φ)$ $(A > 0,ω > 0,0 < φ < \dfrac {π }{2})$, the maximum value of $y=f(x)$ is $2$, the distance between the adjacent symmetry axes of the graph is $2$, and it passes through the point $(1,2)$.
(I) Find $ϕ$;
(II) Calculate $f(1)+f(2)+…+f(2008)$.

Given the function $f(x)=\ln x+ax$.  
$(1)$ If the tangent line to the curve $f(x)$ at the point $(1,f(1))$ is parallel to the line $y=4x+1$, find the value of $a$;  
$(2)$ Discuss the monotonicity of the function $f(x)$.

