b) Each player has two pieces, and the board length is $N>4$ cells;

c) Each player has three pieces, and the board length is $N>6$ cells;

d) Additional challenge: One might think that numerical advantage determines the game's outcome. However, devise and illustrate a board position where White has fewer pieces than Black, but White starts (with a simple move) and wins.

